{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style","id":957557,"title":"Solar Hero Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-25T06:20:19-07:00","id":957557,"title":"Solar Hero Style","content":"Ok am I wrong or is Solar Hero Style completely missing from 3rd ed. Is there a reason for it, like did they get rid of it completely or are they bringing it out later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:29:50-07:00","id":957561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style#post957557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok am I wrong or is Solar Hero Style completely missing from 3rd ed. Is there a reason for it, like did they get rid of it completely or are they bringing it out later?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Solar Hero Style was rolled into the Brawl Charms? Someone who knows the Ex3 Solar charm set can correct me if I am wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:35:45-07:00","id":957564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style?p=957561#post957561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe Solar Hero Style was rolled into the Brawl Charms? Someone who knows the Ex3 Solar charm set can correct me if I am wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong. Most of the Solar Hero charms are in Brawl using the same names as in 2nd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:51:12-07:00","id":957575,"title":"","content":"Solar Hero Style was 2e's take on 1e's Solar Brawl, since 2e had rolled Brawl and MA into one Ability. Now that Brawl is back to being a separate thing, there's no need for SHS whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:52:10-07:00","id":957578,"title":"","content":"I think that Ex2 Solar Hero Style is actually Ex1 Solar Brawl charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:01:13-07:00","id":957584,"title":"","content":"Now I'm remembering how one of the attempts of the Dawn Solution to patch the fact that the native Solar Martial Art was notably weak compared to their other Charms with the idea of giving them a bunch of effects that were exclusive to Solars (I think Infernal Monster did something similar).<br /> <br /> \u200bSo for Third Edition, they rolled that back one way by turning the idea of Hero Styles back into Brawl Charms, and the other by applying the same principle to <i>every</i> Martial Art.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:04:39-07:00","id":957593,"title":"","content":"Hero Styles were an odd duck anyway, since one splat would see it as &quot;just my native unarmed Charms,&quot; while another would see it as &quot;a fighting style that emulates a [x],&quot; as nonsensical as that was (especially when [x] can fight however the hell he wants).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:34:32-07:00","id":957612,"title":"","content":"So nothing like solar hero from now i guess, well that's a little disappointing, I wonder if they are going to do the same with dark messiah, or the violet briers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:54:01-07:00","id":957620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style?p=957612#post957612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So nothing like solar hero from now i guess, well that's a little disappointing, I wonder if they are going to do the same with dark messiah, or the violet briers</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Nothing like...?&quot; What do you mean? Do you want comparatively simple unarmed combat charms to be their own martial art?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:14:23-07:00","id":957626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style?p=957612#post957612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So nothing like solar hero from now i guess, well that's a little disappointing, I wonder if they are going to do the same with dark messiah, or the violet briers</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Solar Hero Style is still there. You just need to be a Solar and take brawl to access it.<br /> <br /> Spoilered to avoid shocking the Rules Lawyers<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I suppose you could copy the Brawl Charms into their own MA if you want a non-Solar to have access to the Solar Hero Style. You will have balance issues to deal with, but what you do at your own gaming table is your own business. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm going to guess Dark Messiah is going the same way for Abyssals. Violet Briers is complicated. My wild theory is Violet Briers will be rolled into Sidereal Melee and Throne Shadow will become Sidereal Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 08-25-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:23:04-07:00","id":957695,"title":"","content":"Violet Bier was a style in 1e as well, so I'd say its chances of remaining one are pretty solid.<br /> <br /> OP, what is it in particular that you miss about the Hero Styles? Did your group make regular use of them in their role as external martial arts rather than an entry point to native MA Charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:36:56-07:00","id":957816,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I suppose the loss of Solar Hero Style as a style is the inability to have your Lunar or Sidereal yell out &quot;HEAVEN THUNDER HAMMER&quot; and punch a motherfucker over the horizon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:35:12-07:00","id":957847,"title":"","content":"...I don't see anything preventing anyone developing an MA emulating solars. It could be part SHS, part... whatever you happen to feel best exemplifies Solars.<br /> <br /> I for one never got the thematic relevance of the SHS grapple and tossing people around charms. Compared to things like Pillar Breaking Blow and Heaven Thunder Hammer, both of which thematically made a lot of sense with the overall image of &quot;greatest and strongest thing going smash&quot;<br /> <br /> but hey, always remember the first rule of RPGs: Nothing has to be set in stone. You can always change things","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:43:39-07:00","id":957851,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of making a martial style to emulate the Solars would probably be difficult when most of them are gone for 1,500 years, but I'll admit I think making Solar Hero/its equivalents into the native Brawl charms was a good call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:57:54-07:00","id":957861,"title":"","content":"Violet Bier's been a style since 1e, so I think it will return. Dark Messiah not so sure. It has a snazzy name so maybe in some form (in name only).<br /> <br /> I think if we wanted to we could write up our own style of MA based around boxing and wrestling, sunlight, glowing kamehamehas and being an athletic, cocky fighter. I don't know if you'd call it Solar Hero though or come up with some other name for it. Shining Sun Style or something. I don't know if that's necessarily any odder than having both Immaculate MA and Dragonblooded native brawl. Maybe that will happen in print some day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:05:18-07:00","id":957863,"title":"","content":"I think either Robert Vance or Lucy Darling suggested that Violet Bier will still be a MA style in a thread about swordsmanship styles. They mentioned it in a list with other martial arts styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:15:05-07:00","id":957906,"title":"","content":"First Edition Sidereals already had Brawl Charms. With the return of Brawl, these Charms will resume their appropriate place as Brawl Charms, where Second Edition instead made them into expansions for Violet Bier of Sorrows.<br /> <br /> Some of the expansion Charms for Throne Shadow Style might become 3rd Edition Brawl Charms, but otherwise Throne Shadow Style might just become a Style that anyone can learn.<br /> <br /> Violet Bier of Sorrows need not even affect the slightest idea of being native to the Sidereal Exalted. It can just be a Style that happens to emulate Saturn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:39:28-07:00","id":957915,"title":"","content":"The idea of converting Solar Brawl into a Martial Art was brought up before. I would hold that doing so would require a fair amount of adaptation, since I find Martial Arts to be constructed in distinct ways that Solar Brawl does not really adhere to (not even accounting for its length), and that are necessary to Martial Arts not only to maintain their texture, but to give them some focus in design and application that helps hold them together outside of the powers of any given Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:29:45-07:00","id":957970,"title":"","content":"Dang. Now this has me thinking. I'm seriously tempted to put together a really hammy Dragon-Blooded who fights with a style (unknowingly, to him!) inspired by the stereotypical Solar brawler, just to see the indignation on my Circle's face when he shouts &quot;HEAVEN THUNDER HAMMER&quot; and punches the Zenith through a tree.<br /> <br /> What sort of name would you give that style, though? Impetuous Protagonist Style is maybe a little too on the nose, but it suggests to me a spectacularly theatrical style with social influence the precise opposite of Black Claw. You do less damage than it appears, and everyone is very impressed with how imposing and capable you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:57:01-07:00","id":957988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style?p=957612#post957612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So nothing like solar hero from now i guess, well that's a little disappointing, I wonder if they are going to do the same with dark messiah, or the violet briers</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Messiah was made from Abyssal Brawl Charms that were forced to pretend to be a Martial Art Style. It was just as bad for them as it was for Solar Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:19:14-07:00","id":958183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style?p=957695#post957695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Violet Bier was a style in 1e as well, so I'd say its chances of remaining one are pretty solid.<br /> <br /> OP, what is it in particular that you miss about the Hero Styles? Did your group make regular use of them in their role as external martial arts rather than an entry point to native MA Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I used it as an entry point for people learning martial arts. I'm a martial artist myself and i used it as a this is the basic foundation of martial arts, end then used the other styles to show a persons focus in a particular facet of martial arts. It's what I know so that's why I used it like that so it would make sense to me so i could be comfortable running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","user":"Eric Ericson","date":". 08-26-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:03:01-07:00","id":958298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style?p=958183#post958183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used it as an entry point for people learning martial arts. I'm a martial artist myself and i used it as a this is the basic foundation of martial arts, end then used the other styles to show a persons focus in a particular facet of martial arts. It's what I know so that's why I used it like that so it would make sense to me so i could be comfortable running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brawl still works that way, effectively. Everyone gets Brawl, and then you can take a Merit to learn a MA. The same general ass-kicking techniques are present; they just removed the conceit that it was a distinct Style that came naturally to some Exalts and not to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:33:57-07:00","id":958513,"title":"","content":"The trouble with that approach is that you cannot use both Brawl and MA charms together. This can of course be fixed with a simple house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3558-dunecat","name":"dunecat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:46:10-07:00","id":958547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dunecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/957557-solar-hero-style?p=958513#post958513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This can of course be fixed with a simple house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as simple as you think, unless you're cool with your game fantastically self-destructing the first time your players combine Brawl with Tiger Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T19:30:47-07:00","id":958566,"title":"","content":"Abyssals learnin Solar Hero be like<br /> <img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/skjBqq4xEFakULC22F2cNJE4Q3AF7uXbhjWRgor9Do5H8Kn2n_x0724Q_vATe8wZ41OhT20-MNP64AblOIY_5jkMY8f3fdOIqO4Q9psO2ak7CEB5ndUmKRGhkTI22bMaHoyihLRedfeCyAtme7lMG_GAl_YNSBNrfpAi88JCJKrBEy5UP5qZtkJZK3HQzmPFL5UxKQP3PqIwEri4fqz5qAr45m5hgozC0aGHcMlHk0_fwXLQGcX4cDjG_lc7UOnn8S6vKQFlPeOIq40VaVH_EKX7ZM2LxbAgEVgula2Owbsx3TzbYwdquFxlIMndidgciO_5LpKmy7mleW32O2ZYtuJd0tWansm6akGENzUWrwk58O04MztB1Zv0CpKZS-N8FJifu-dm3UNqfQS66Mz590uYsz5epczx79mPz1ptUHpnr-1UL9IDzSvRC9kJ1Z-nNBvOXZZMlwREWr1